Here is an OWL ontology design pattern (ODP) in Turtle syntax that encodes the scenario and answers the competency questions:
```turtle
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>.
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>.
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.
@prefix :     <http://example.org/odp#>.

:Ontology a owl:Ontology ;
rdfs:label "Sprinkler Use Case Ontology" ;
rdfs:comment "An ontology for representing the causal relations between events in the sprinkler use case scenario".

; Scenario-requirement-to-axiom mapping

; 1. It is rainy season.
:RainySeason a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Rainy Season" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of it being rainy season".

; 2. The sprinkler is on.
:SprinklerOn a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Sprinkler On" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of the sprinkler being on".

; 3. It is raining.
:Raining a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Raining" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of it raining".

; 4. The pavement is wet.
:PavementWet a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Pavement Wet" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of the pavement being wet".

; 5. The pavement is slippery.
:PavementSlippery a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Pavement Slippery" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of the pavement being slippery".

; Competency Questions-to-axiom mapping

; 1. What events are responsible for the pavement being slippery?
:PavementSlippery a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Pavement Slippery" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of the pavement being slippery".

:SlipperyPavement a owl:ObjectProperty ;
rdfs:label "Slippery Pavement" ;
rdfs:comment "An object property representing the relation between the pavement being slippery and the events that cause it".

:RainySeason :SlipperyPavement :PavementWet.
:SprinklerOn :SlipperyPavement :PavementWet.
:Raining :SlipperyPavement :PavementWet.

; 2. What would be the outcome of turning the sprinkler system on(off)?
:SprinklerOn a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Sprinkler On" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of the sprinkler being on".

:SprinklerOff a owl:Class ;
rdfs:label "Sprinkler Off" ;
rdfs:comment "A class representing the event of the sprinkler being off".

:SprinklerState a owl:ObjectProperty ;
rdfs:label "Sprinkler State" ;
rdfs:comment "An object property representing the relation between the sprinkler and its state".

:SprinklerOn :SprinklerState :On.
:SprinklerOff :SprinklerState :Off.

; 3. How strong is the causal link between the sprinkler being on and the pavement being wet?
:CausalLink a owl:ObjectProperty ;
rdfs:label "Causal Link" ;
rdfs:comment "An object property representing the causal relation between two events".

:SprinklerOn :CausalLink :